N:agent-reach
D:Operate Panniantong/Agent-Reach, the MIT-licensed installer, doctor, and routing layer for platform-specific internet research tools. Use when the user names Agent Reach, agent-reach, its channel doctor, optional backend setup, OpenCLI integration, cookie configuration, transcription, or an Agent Reach update or uninstall. Choose fit-check, offline preflight, scoped setup, channel routing, credential handoff, transcription, or maintenance. Preserve existing skills: upstream installation can replace the same-named agent-reach skill. Require explicit approval for installs, credential access, browser/session integration, Docker changes, paid uploads, and deletion. Route generic crawling to scrapling and existing authenticated browser tasks to the browser or platform skill.
U[7]:
  Fit-check a named platform and select one bounded read route
  Inspect host presence and selected source fingerprints without executing upstream
  Prepare approval-gated pinned package and backend setup
  Diagnose a trusted installed channel and verify a real read
  Scope cookie handoff and existing browser-session integration
  Approve audio upload provider cost and fallback separately
  Update or remove deliberately while preserving same-named skills
S[7]{n,action,details}:
  1,Select mode,Setup and doctor layer; retrieval belongs to external backends
  2,Preflight,Use the bundled offline checker and do not read account configuration
  3,Freeze setup,Pin source; check Python 3.10+; preserve existing agent-reach skills
  4,Route read,Use a usable active backend and one bounded query
  5,Authorize credentials,Keep platform and destination explicit; never expose secret values
  6,Authorize upload,Select transcription provider and cost before transfer
  7,Verify,Distinguish documents package presence channel readiness and actual retrieval
R[8]:
  No invented agent-reach search/read/fetch commands; bundled MCP is get_status only
  Never run upstream installation or doctor during blanket catalog setup
  System and skill installers may replace this same-named wrapper
  Default safe install checks are not an inert offline inventory
  Automatic browser import is Bilibili/Xueqiu only and needs permission
  XHS Docker cookie copy/restart requires image and destination verification
  Uninstall leaves external tools MCP entries and possible legacy credential copies
  Fingerprints cover listed file bytes only; mismatch requires review not auto-acceptance
E[3]{desc,in,out}:
  "Preserve skills","install Agent Reach without changing skills","offline report then approved package-only setup"
  "Private audio","transcribe with any provider","confirm rights upload provider and cost; no silent fallback"
  "Generic crawl","crawl arbitrary websites","route to scrapling or existing browser owner"
